    {
      "id": "qbqz9l9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to the Supreme Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Supreme Court of India stands at the apex of the Indian judicial system under Part V of the Constitution.",
        "Original Jurisdiction under Article 131 covers disputes between the Union and States or among States.",
        "Advisory Jurisdiction under Article 143 authorizes the President to consult the Supreme Court on vital questions of law or fact.",
        "Writ Jurisdiction under Article 32 empowers citizens to directly approach the Supreme Court for fundamental rights enforcement.",
        "Judges are appointed by the President of India and hold office until attaining the age of 65 years."
      ],
      "id": "ncv6prg"
    },
